@startuml pub-c4-container
' C4 Level 2 — Container — Publication (PUB)
title Cordelê — Publication (PUB) — Container

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #24608A
}

rectangle "BFF (NestJS)\nsingle entry point" as BFF
rectangle "Cordelê backend (NestJS 11 monolith)" as App {
  rectangle "PubModule\n(pub bounded context)" as PUB #E8F0FE
  rectangle "ImpModule" as IMP
  rectangle "CompModule" as COMP
  rectangle "ProjModule" as PROJ
}
database "PostgreSQL 16\n(Prisma; tenant schema emp_<slug>)" as PG
rectangle "File Storage\n(FileStoragePort adapter:\nlocal disk / S3)" as Storage
rectangle "epubcheck JAR\n(EpubValidationPort adapter:\nchild process)" as EpubCheck

BFF --> PUB : POST /api/pub/projetos/{id}/publicacoes (202)\nGET .../status (poll), .../download, .../stats
PUB --> IMP : in-process DI\n(ManuscriptContentPort.getContentTree)
PUB --> COMP : in-process DI\n(GetMetadados / GetConfiguracaoLayout)
PUB --> PROJ : in-process DI\n(AdvanceProjetoStatusUseCase.advanceTo)
PUB --> PG : Prisma repository\n(publicacao, validation_message; tenant schema)
PUB --> Storage : put/get/delete/signUrl\n(tenant-scoped keys)
PUB ..> EpubCheck : validate(ocf) -> verdict\n(child process)
PROJ ..> PUB : PublicationHistoryPort / PublicationErasurePort\n(in-process DI)

note right of PUB
  No Kafka/Artemis (messaging.enabled=false) -> progress via polling.
  No Eureka/gateway (single monolith).
  epubcheck (JVM) is the only Java: an external tool behind a port,
  not a service dependency (TECH-001 stands for the service code).
end note
@enduml
